From: nixos-rk3588 contributors
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: rockchip: fix NanoPi R6C PCIe node removal

The R6C uses the second PCIe lane for M.2 instead of the R6S's second
RTL8125. Commit 6063a18b4c01 ("arm64: dts: rockchip: fixes warning in
pci_device_reg for nanopi-r6 series") renamed the inherited PCI bridge
node to pcie@0,0 without updating the R6C deletion. Remove the renamed
node so the R6S-only endpoint is not described on the M.2 lane.

Source: https://github.com/armbian/linux-rockchip/commit/6063a18b4c01
Applies to: b908c7339f51eddcfe8402cd15d1e1f8f4e67c29
The existing DTS retains its (GPL-2.0+ OR MIT) license and copyrights.

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588s-nanopi-r6c.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588s-nanopi-r6c.dts
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588s-nanopi-r6c.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588s-nanopi-r6c.dts
@@ -28,2 +28,2 @@
-	/delete-node/ pcie@40;
+	/delete-node/ pcie@0,0;
 };
